findings.body:
Before this PR, `getOutputRecurringSeatedBookings` returned results sorted by `start`. The PR replaced that with `return transformed;`, and the change has nothing to do with `displayEmail`:

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="411-425"}

The output follows the order of `bookingsIds`. Those IDs come from `bookingsRepository.getRecurringByUidWithAttendeesAndUserAndEvent(uid)` (bookings.service.ts ~L602-611), and that `findMany` has no `orderBy`. Postgres doesn't promise any row order without one, so `GET /v2/bookings/{recurringUid}` for a recurring seated event can return occurrences in arbitrary order. This is also now inconsistent with the sibling `getOutputRecurringBookings` (L243) and `getOutputCreateRecurringSeatedBookings` (L448), which both still sort.

::callout{type="warning"}
Clients that read `data[0]` as the first occurrence will silently get the wrong booking. Seated e2e tests that index `firstBooking`/`secondBooking` may also become flaky.

::suggestion{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="424-424"}
    return transformed.sort((a, b) => new Date(a.start).getTime() - new Date(b.start).getTime());

`BookingAttendee.cleanEmailForDisplay` is never called anywhere (grep finds only its definition). It copies the regex from `OutputBookingsService_2024_08_13.getDisplayEmail`, which leaves two sources of truth that can drift. It also puts logic on a DTO class that is otherwise purely declarative.

::diff{file="packages/platform/types/bookings/2024-08-13/outputs/booking.output.ts" lines="58-62"}

Remove it. If a shared helper is wanted, export one function (e.g. from `@calcom/platform-libraries` or a small util) and use it in output.service.ts and google-calendar.service.ts, which already has the same regex.

The same two `if` blocks are pasted into both `getOutputBooking` and `getOutputRecurringBooking`. The copies already differ: one passes the unbound method reference `.map(this.getDisplayEmail)`, the other uses `.map((guest: string) => this.getDisplayEmail(guest))`.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="158-174"}

The unbound version works today only because `getDisplayEmail` doesn't touch `this`. If someone later moves the regex onto an instance field, it will throw at runtime. Pull this into one private helper:

::suggestion{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="158-174"}
    this.addDisplayEmailsToResponses(bookingTransformed.bookingFieldsResponses);

Then implement `addDisplayEmailsToResponses(responses)` once, with the arrow-function form.

`/\+[a-zA-Z0-9]{25}/` matches the first `+` followed by 25 alphanumerics anywhere in the string, and it doesn't require the `@` to come right after.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="96-98"}

Examples:
- A real attendee `alice+newsletterssubscriptions2024@example.com` becomes `alice2024@example.com`. The result is a different, wrong address, not just the same address without its tag.
- A non-managed attendee whose tag happens to be exactly 25 alphanumerics loses the tag.

The pattern matches existing code (google-calendar.service.ts), but this field is now public API output, so a lookahead is cheap insurance. Managed-user suffixes always sit directly before `@`.

::suggestion{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="96-98"}
  private getDisplayEmail(email: string): string {
    return email.replace(/\+[a-zA-Z0-9]{25}(?=@)/, "");
  }

The PR says the OpenAPI spec was auto-updated, but four `"required": [` lines are now at column 0 (L31729, L31833, L32267, L33370). Generated output wouldn't look like that. The next real regeneration will produce diff noise, and if the spec was hand-edited it may not match what `@ApiProperty` generates. For example, `displayEmail` on `SeatedAttendee` is inherited, so check that the generated spec includes it.

::diff{file="docs/api-reference/v2/openapi.json" lines="31726-31736"}

Regenerate the spec with the project's swagger generation script rather than editing it by hand.
